{"seq":20,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/hermes-opus-gbrain-labelled-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T19:44:03.450Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"18a08a8051c117d9ef2020fd34844ccb32575803cd4d784180da1513052bf9d8","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. #PD-4492: Eau Claire yard. Gatehouse kiosk SMS bay assignments weren't reaching drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14-18. Support patched it 4 Oct 2025 and Thea confirmed the fix on 5 Oct. Source: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). It's listed under What Changed, and again as a 6 Oct action item to archive the kiosk logs.\n\n2. #4419: Gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. Source: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Because the note has no date, I can't tell you when this was current.\n\nI also checked Moss's other notes: the 14 Sep 2025 North pipeline digest, the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in and the two Central digests. None of them has a QFL ticket number. The cheat sheet notes that Quarendon Freightways (one r) is a different company and not a customer, so I left it out.\n\nThere are other QFL tickets outside Moss's notes, like SUP-4471 (the Nov 2025 Sev 1) and #4912 on the account page. I can add those as a separate list if you want them in the weekly notes.","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"}}
